1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,070
Okay, okay — new idea. Hear me out. Um…
no, wait. This one's actually big.

2
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:08,630
So… did we make it?

3
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:09,890
Read it.

4
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:12,500
It's blank.

5
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:16,080
We don't write things down. We talk. Voice
notes, all day, every idea.

6
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:17,800
What happened to that guy?

7
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:20,270
I don't know how it ends yet.

8
00:00:20,310 --> 00:00:22,170
Then don't write it. Say it.

9
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:25,800
Okay. Did we build anything?

10
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:27,230
Three things.

11
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:28,570
Three companies?

12
00:00:28,610 --> 00:00:31,110
Three products. Calm down.

13
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:32,770
…Okay. First one.

14
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:38,410
Friends were throwing around a hackathon
idea. I shipped it in four, five hours.

15
00:00:38,450 --> 00:00:44,300
Two, three days later I'd bought a domain
— didn't even know how domains worked.

16
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:48,230
Ten emails. One reply.

17
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:49,560
One reply!

18
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:55,400
Wrong customers. Small sites didn't feel
the pain. Big ones already had someone.

19
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:56,280
Second?

20
00:00:56,320 --> 00:01:01,270
Spending limits for AI apps. Nobody cared
about the bill yet.

21
00:01:01,310 --> 00:01:02,100
Third?

22
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:07,770
Safety rules for AI agents. Five months.
Best thing I've ever built.

23
00:01:07,810 --> 00:01:11,825
You sleep at twelve, right? I was up till
three. Every night.

24
00:01:11,865 --> 00:01:13,620
Code, customers, emails.

25
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:15,210
So who's using it?

26
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:20,010
Fifty emails. Zero replies.

27
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:22,450
Did you try—

28
00:01:22,490 --> 00:01:28,222
Articles. Reddit. One post blew up in a
few hours. Mods took it down.

29
00:01:28,262 --> 00:01:29,860
Account too new.

30
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:31,590
…Of course they did.

31
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:33,310
Money?

32
00:01:33,350 --> 00:01:34,580
Zero.

33
00:01:35,830 --> 00:01:40,970
I'd promised myself five thousand dollars
a month. By December.

34
00:01:41,010 --> 00:01:46,285
Placements are next July. Half of me is
preparing for that. Half of me is here.

35
00:01:46,325 --> 00:01:47,460
Never all in.

36
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:50,900
So two months ago, I stopped. Everything.

37
00:01:51,950 --> 00:01:55,700
Was I wrong? To want it that big?

38
00:01:55,750 --> 00:02:03,090
No. You're the only reason I started. You
just didn't know how long the middle is.

39
00:02:03,130 --> 00:02:08,191
I kept asking AI for ideas. But real
problems don't come from prompts.

40
00:02:08,231 --> 00:02:13,520
They come from people. And I've been doing
it all alone, in one room.

41
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:14,890
So what's next?

42
00:02:14,930 --> 00:02:18,884
Get out of this room. Talk to people.
Maybe physical AI.

43
00:02:18,924 --> 00:02:21,200
Honestly, I don't know yet.

44
00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:22,400
It's okay.

45
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:23,350
…What?

46
00:02:23,390 --> 00:02:25,150
It's okay. You'll do it.

47
00:02:25,190 --> 00:02:26,550
How do you know?

48
00:02:26,590 --> 00:02:28,520
You're still talking to me.

49
00:02:30,570 --> 00:02:33,400
Don't write it. Say it.

50
00:02:34,450 --> 00:02:37,010
Okay. New idea. Hear me out.
